---
import DashboardMock from "./DashboardMock.astro";
---

<section class="story" id="rhythm">
  <div class="wrap story__grid">
    <div class="story__pin">
      <DashboardMock />
      <p class="story__caption">Stays beside the work. Counts only while you are at the screen.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="story__chapters">
      <article>
        <p class="kicker"><span class="kicker__dot"></span>Why it exists</p>
        <h2 class="display">Your eyes work hard for you. Screens make them work worse.</h2>
        <p>
          During focused computer use, people blink far less often than they do
          in conversation. That drop is a well-known driver of digital eye
          strain: dryness, grit, fatigue, and blurred vision.
        </p>
        <p>
          The problem is not that you “forget to care.” Attention narrows, the
          face stills, and blinking becomes sparse and uneven — and you rarely
          notice until the eyes already hurt.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <p class="kicker"><span class="kicker__dot"></span>What rhythm means</p>
        <h2 class="display">Rate and regularity, together.</h2>
        <p>
          Rate answers how often. Regularity answers how steady. Either one
          alone is incomplete: enough blinks can still arrive in bursts and
          droughts, and a perfectly even but very slow pattern still leaves the
          surface under-refreshed.
        </p>
        <p>
          EyeRhythm folds both into the <strong>Ocular Rhythm Index</strong> —
          a 0–100 glance for “is my blink cadence supporting me right now?” A
          healthy desk cadence is often around 15–20 blinks per minute.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <p class="kicker"><span class="kicker__dot"></span>The companion</p>
        <h2 class="display">It watches, scores, and, if you ask, gently nudges.</h2>
        <p>
          Live rate, regularity, and ORI on a compact window. Optional alert if
          ORI stays low for a meaningful stretch — not a single bad second.
          Optional beep on each counted blink. Practice is a two-minute
          full-screen coach so the habit is easier to feel, not only to measure.
        </p>
        <p>
          It is a wellness companion, not a medical device. Persistent
          discomfort or a change in vision belongs with a licensed eye-care
          professional.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .story {
    background: var(--band);
    padding: clamp(48px, 8vw, 96px) 0;
  }

  .story__grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 40px;
  }

  .story__pin {
    display: none;
  }

  .story__chapters {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  article {
    display: grid;
    gap: 16px;
    justify-items: start;
    padding: 28px 0 48px;
  }

  article p {
    color: var(--text-soft);
    max-width: 38rem;
  }

  article strong {
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .story__caption {
    margin-top: 16px;
    font-size: 0.86rem;
    color: var(--text-soft);
    text-align: center;
    max-width: 22rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 980px) {
    .story__grid {
      grid-template-columns: 0.9fr 1.1fr;
      align-items: start;
      gap: 64px;
    }

    .story__pin {
      display: grid;
      justify-items: center;
      position: sticky;
      top: calc(var(--nav-h) + 36px);
    }

    article {
      min-height: 72vh;
      align-content: center;
      padding: 48px 0;
    }
  }
</style>
